---
description: Захватить в хранилище исходной базы изменённые объекты ветки
agent: code
---

Use this command only from an active ready configuration `itldev/*` worktree whose source infobase uses a configuration repository.

Run the helper directly from the current project directory:

If the agent shell tool supports `timeout_ms`, run this lifecycle command with `timeout_ms >= 3900000` by default so the outer shell outlives the 3600-second 1C Designer/Enterprise limit. Do not use `120000 ms` or another short default.

```powershell
powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\.agents\skills\1c-workflow\scripts\run-itl-command.ps1 -- -Action lock-config-repository-objects
```

The helper maps committed, staged, unstaged, deleted, and untracked configuration delta to an official XML object list and invokes only `/ConfigurationRepositoryLock -Objects` against the source infobase. It never loads configuration files and never widens the request to the full configuration. An empty list is a successful no-op; unresolved paths block before Designer starts. Return a non-empty `userReport` exactly, including when `status=failed`: it preserves successful captures, conflicting owners, absent objects and unconfirmed outcomes. Apply the same `userReportOmitted` file recovery on failure as on success. Preserve the failed status and append its `requiredAction`; do not replace a partial report with only the first conflict or automatically retry/unlock objects. If no report exists and `LOCK_CONFIG_REPOSITORY_OBJECT_CONFLICT` already names the exact objects and repository users, report that error and its `requiredAction` directly without reading `console.log`. For other failures without a report, read only the last 80 lines of `logPath`.
